n properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Accept all' button. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by making new choices in the menu. Click on 'Overview' at the top for a complete overview of the cookies in each category. Please see our cookies page for more information and to reset your cookie preferences. Functional Analytics Marketing & Social Media Reject all Accept Selection Accept all Eur.nl Functional Cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary for the website to work, such as remembering your preferences, security, enabling log-in or processing forms. Consent Studio Consent Studio consent-studio__consent-id ID of the proof of consent storage within the Consent Studio platform. 30 days consent-studio__storage Local storage for the consent given by the user for certain categories of cookies. 30 days consent-studio__seen Boolean that keeps track of whether the user has seen the cookie banner at least once. 30 days consent-studio__implicit-consent-triggered When a website has implicit consent configured, this cookie stores whether or not it has been triggered or not. 30 days consent-studio__gpc-consent-triggered Records that your browser's Global Privacy Control signal was detected, so non-essential cookies were automatically declined on your behalf. 30 days LinkedIn LinkedIn li_gc Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes 2 years Cloudflare Cloudflare __cf_bm Cloudflare's bot products identify and mitigate automated traffic to protect your site from bad bots. Cloudflare places the __cf_bm cookie on End User devices that access Customer sites that are protected by Bot Management or Bot Fight Mode. The __cf_bm cookie is necessary for the proper functioning of these bot solutions. Session _cfuvid The _cfuvid cookie is only set when a site uses this option in a Rate Limiting Rule, and is only used to allow the Cloudflare WAF to distinguish individual users who share the same IP address. Session cf_clearance Whether a CAPTCHA or Javascript challenge has been solved. Session HubSpot HubSpot hs_sessionid* Identifies your current visit so HubSpot can keep your session consistent while you browse. — Google Google __Secure-ENID Used by Google to prevent fraudulent login attempts. This also contains a Google user ID which can be used for statistics and marketing purposes following a successful login 11 months Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Hotjar cookie that is set when a user first lands on a page with the Hotjar script. It is used to persist the Hotjar User ID, unique to that site on the browser. This ensures that behavior in subsequent visits to the same site will be attributed to the same user ID. 365 days _hjSession_* A cookie that holds the current session data. This ensues that subsequent requests within the session window will be attributed to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Erasmus University Rotterdam CMS personalisation.segments This collects anonymous data about which category a visitor fits into. This allows us to offer the visitor content that matches their profile, based on visiting behaviour. — OnlineAfspraken.nl OnlineAfspraken.nl booking widget oa-dao-Resource* Stores the list of bookable resources, such as staff or rooms, that the appointment widget can offer. — oa-dao-ConsumerForm* Stores the layout and field definitions of the booking form, not the details you enter. — oa-dao-AppTypeGroup* Stores the categories used to group appointment types in the booking widget. — oa-booking Stores the details of the appointment you are currently booking. — oa-dao-* Stores appointment widget reference data on your device so the booking form does not have to reload it on every visit. — oa-application-widget-booking-consumerwidget-state Stores technical state the booking widget needs to work. — oa-dao-Mailing-MailingList-* Stores a mailing list that the appointment widget can offer you to subscribe to. — oa-configHash Stores a code used to check whether the booking widget has changed, so out-of-date saved booking data can be cleared. — oa-consumer Stores the identity of the signed-in customer for the booking. — oa-dao-AppType* Stores the list of appointment types the booking widget can offer. — oa-shoppingcart Stores the items you have added to your booking basket. — Analytics These cookies and similar technologies collect information about how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited most, whether errors occur, and how users interact, to help us measure performance and improve the site. Google Google Analytics _ga ID used to identify users 2 years FPID Registers statistical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. — FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. — _ga_* ID used to identify users 2 years eur.nl Website *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. — *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. — *_FPAU Records which audience segments Google Analytics has assigned to you, used for reporting on visitor groups. — Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google _gcl_au Used by Google AdSense for experimenting with advertisement efficiency across websites using their services. 3 months NID This cookies is used to collect website statistics and track conversion rates and Google ad personalisation 1 year Google Analytics FPAU Assigns a specific ID to the visitor. This allows the website to determine the number of specific user-visits for analysis and statistics. Session DoubleClick/Google Marketing IDE This cookie is used for targeting, analyzing and optimisation of ad campaigns in DoubleClick/Google Marketing Suite 2 years Google Ads _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Used by the social networking service, LinkedIn, for tracking the use of embedded services. 1 day bcookie Used by LinkedIn to track the use of embedded services. 1 year Facebook Facebook _fbp Used by Facebook to deliver a series of advertisement products such as real time bidding from third party advertisers 4 months eur.nl Website *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — *__gcl_au Stores the identifier of the advert you clicked, so a later purchase or sign-up can be credited to the right campaign. — Meta Meta Pixel lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
