    "https://www.eur.nl/en/working-at-eur/vacancies/tutor-academy-ay-2526": {
      "title": "Tutor Academy AY 25/26",
      "description": "Tutor Academy AY 25/26 | Working at | Erasmus University Rotterdam Skip to main content Skip to search Skip to subnavigation Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Close Open search Close Open menu Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Switch language to EN English current language NL Nederlands Search Close Search Search Featured results Primary Why work at EUR Open submenu Why work at EUR Campus Diversity Societal involvement Sustainability Working conditions Working areas Open submenu Working areas Academic staff Working in Finance Working in IT Working at Legal Affairs Working at Real Estate & Facilities PhD LDE traineeship International staff Practical information Open submenu Practical information Candidate portal Vacancies Tutor Academy AY 25/26 Listen Published Friday 22 Aug 2025 Work area Education Organisational unit Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) Salary € 3.230 Employment 0.1 fte - 0.5 fte Introduction As a Tutor Academy teaching assistant, you work with the various researchers, lecturers and/or professors at Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM) Opens external . Job description In your role as teaching assistant (TA), you support faculty in conducting research or with their administrative tasks. You may also grade assignments and/or exams and give workshops. We provide you with additional training so that you can deliver workshops when needed. Please note: first-year students cannot apply for a TA vacancy and alumni typically do not serve as teaching assistants. Job requirements Before you can apply for a Tutor Academy vacancy, you must: reside in the Netherlands; and possess a BSN (social security number). Employment conditions and benefits You are compensated according to the standard student-assistant scale. In autumn 2023, for example, this amounted to a gross hourly rate of between €15.87 and €15.90 for second- and third-year students, and €17.24 - €17.28 for fourth-year and master students. Please note: although we have compiled the salary scales with the utmost care, the final numbers may deviate from the scale based on the contract we offer to you (via HR or EURFlex). Employer Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR) is an internationally oriented university with a strong social orientation in its education and research, as expressed in our mission ‘Creating positive societal impact’. EUR is home to 4,100 academics and professionals and almost 33,000 students from more than 140 countries. Everything we do, we do under the credo The Erasmian Way – Making Minds Matter. We’re global citizens, connecting, entrepreneurial, open-minded, and socially involved. These Erasmian Values function as our internal compass and create EUR’s distinctive and recognizable profile. From these values, with a broad perspective and with an eye for diversity, different backgrounds and opinions, our employees work closely together to solve societal challenges from the dynamic and cosmopolitan city of Rotterdam. Thanks to the high quality and positive societal impact of our research and education, EUR can compete with the top European universities. www.eur.nl . Faculty / Institute / Central service Rotterdam School of Management, Erasmus University (RSM) is one of Europe’s top-ranked business schools. RSM provides ground-breaking research and education furthering excellence in all aspects of management and is based in the international port city of Rotterdam – a vital nexus of business, logistics and trade. RSM’s primary focus is on developing business leaders with international careers who can become a force for positive change by carrying their innovative mindset into a sustainable future. Our first-class range of bachelor, master, MBA, PhD and executive programmes encourage them to become critical, creative, caring and collaborative thinkers and doers. www.rsm.nl Opens external Applying Please go to “Apply for this vacancy” in the header above to register for the Tutor Academy. Be sure to use your private email address, so that we can send you regular updates about the teaching assistant opportunities that have become available and align with your competences. Upon registration, you immediately receive an email to confirm your membership within our candidate pool. Haven’t received the confirmation email? Please contact us for assistance at tutoracademy@rsm.nl . You are under no obligation to accept any of the offered assignments; you can disregard any vacancies that do not align with your interests. Important: please understand that registration alone does not qualify you for any TA positions. You must follow the given instructions to apply to the individual emailed vacancies that interest you. Want to unregister at any point? You can do that via the candidate portal Opens external . For any inquiries or clarifications, please contact us at tutoracademy@rsm.nl Stay up to date with new vacancies! Want to be the first to know about vacancies that match your interests? Let us know what you're looking for, and we'll send you an email as soon as a new opportunity that fits your profile is posted.\nDon’t miss out on your perfect job! Sign up Close Stay up to date with new vacancies! Job alert Please select your preferences. When a new job becomes available that matches these preference we'll send you an email. Fields marked with a * are required. First Name Last Name Email address Password Your password requires a minimum of 8 characters of which 2 non-alphabetic Confirm password Business Unit Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) Any Any Erasmus School of Economics (ESE) Erasmus School of Law (ESL) Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication (ESHCC) Erasmus School of Social and Behavioural Sciences (ESSB) Erasmus School of Philosophy (ESPhil) Rotterdam School of Management (RSM) International Institute of Social Studies (ISS) Erasmus School of Health Policy & Management (ESHPM) General Management Directorate (ABD) University Library (UB) Convergence Human Resources (HR) Finance (FIN) Education and Student Affairs (E&S) Erasmus Digitalisation and Information Services (EDIS) Real Estate & Facilities (RE&F) Engagement & Research Services (ERS) Marketing & Communications (M&C) RSM BV Institute for Housing and Urban Development Studies (IHS) OK Cancel Expertise Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement Any Any Administration & Secretariat Policy & Advice IT Marketing & Communication Human Resources Finance Legal Real Estate & Facilities Management Education Research, development, innovation Academic staff PhD Procurement OK Cancel Share this page Interested? Apply now Applicant portal Open navigation for Tutor Academy AY 25/26 Close Interested? Apply now Interested? Apply now Compare 0 study programmes Close Compare 0 study programmes 0 of 3 study programmes selected. @title Duration: @duration Remove @title Compare study programmes Breadcrumb Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Vacancies Tutor Academy AY 25/26 Working at Erasmus University Rotterdam Directly to Information Directly to Why work at EUR Working areas International staff Practical information Vacancies Information ANBI Cookies Disclaimer Privacy statement Accessibility Our channels Facebook Instagram X (formerly twitter) Linkedin Youtube Making Minds Matter Watch the video Close Our website uses cookies Overview This website uses cookies and similar technologies (hereinafter collectively: 'cookies'). In this menu, you can choose which types of cookies and purposes you consent to. Functional: ​​These cookies are technically necessary for the website to function properly. Using the website is not possible without accepting these cookies. Analytics: These cookies are used to analyze and improve website usage in general. We take measures to ensure that your privacy is not, or only minimally, affected by these cookies. It's highly appreciated if you toggle the switch. Marketing & Social Media: If you want marketing campaigns and advertisements you see online and on social media to be tailored to your browsing behavior and the interests derived from it, you can enable the slider or click the 'Accept all' button. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by making new choices in the menu. Click on 'Overview' at the top for a complete overview of the cookies in each category. Please see our cookies page for more information and to reset your cookie preferences. Functional Analytics Marketing & Social Media Reject all Accept Selection Accept all Eur.nl Functional Cookies and similar technologies that are strictly necessary for the website to work, such as remembering your preferences, security, enabling log-in or processing forms. Consent Studio Consent Studio consent-studio__consent-id ID of the proof of consent storage within the Consent Studio platform. 30 days consent-studio__storage Local storage for the consent given by the user for certain categories of cookies. 30 days consent-studio__seen Boolean that keeps track of whether the user has seen the cookie banner at least once. 30 days consent-studio__implicit-consent-triggered When a website has implicit consent configured, this cookie stores whether or not it has been triggered or not. 30 days consent-studio__gpc-consent-triggered Records that your browser's Global Privacy Control signal was detected, so non-essential cookies were automatically declined on your behalf. 30 days LinkedIn LinkedIn li_gc Used to store guest consent to the use of cookies for non-essential purposes 2 years Cloudflare Cloudflare __cf_bm Cloudflare's bot products identify and mitigate automated traffic to protect your site from bad bots. Cloudflare places the __cf_bm cookie on End User devices that access Customer sites that are protected by Bot Management or Bot Fight Mode. The __cf_bm cookie is necessary for the proper functioning of these bot solutions. Session _cfuvid The _cfuvid cookie is only set when a site uses this option in a Rate Limiting Rule, and is only used to allow the Cloudflare WAF to distinguish individual users who share the same IP address. Session cf_clearance Whether a CAPTCHA or Javascript challenge has been solved. Session HubSpot HubSpot hs_sessionid* Identifies your current visit so HubSpot can keep your session consistent while you browse. — Google Google __Secure-ENID Used by Google to prevent fraudulent login attempts. This also contains a Google user ID which can be used for statistics and marketing purposes following a successful login 11 months Erasmus University Rotterdam CMS personalisation.segments This collects anonymous data about which category a visitor fits into. This allows us to offer the visitor content that matches their profile, based on visiting behaviour. — OnlineAfspraken.nl OnlineAfspraken.nl booking widget oa-dao-Resource* Stores the list of bookable resources, such as staff or rooms, that the appointment widget can offer. — oa-dao-ConsumerForm* Stores the layout and field definitions of the booking form, not the details you enter. — oa-dao-AppTypeGroup* Stores the categories used to group appointment types in the booking widget. — oa-booking Stores the details of the appointment you are currently booking. — oa-dao-* Stores appointment widget reference data on your device so the booking form does not have to reload it on every visit. — oa-application-widget-booking-consumerwidget-state Stores technical state the booking widget needs to work. — oa-dao-Mailing-MailingList-* Stores a mailing list that the appointment widget can offer you to subscribe to. — oa-configHash Stores a code used to check whether the booking widget has changed, so out-of-date saved booking data can be cleared. — oa-consumer Stores the identity of the signed-in customer for the booking. — oa-dao-AppType* Stores the list of appointment types the booking widget can offer. — oa-shoppingcart Stores the items you have added to your booking basket. — Analytics These cookies and similar technologies collect information about how visitors use our website, such as which pages are visited most, whether errors occur, and how users interact, to help us measure performance and improve the site. Google Google Analytics _ga ID used to identify users 2 years FPID Registers statistical data on users' behaviour on the website. Used for internal analytics by the website operator. — FPLC This FPLC cookie is the cross-domain linker cookie hashed from the FPID cookie. It’s not HttpOnly, which means it can be read with JavaScript. It has a relatively short lifetime, just 20 hours. — _ga_* ID used to identify users 2 years eur.nl Website *__ga_* Keeps track of your current visit for one specific Google Analytics property. — *__ga Identifies your browser so Google Analytics can tell returning visitors from new ones. — *_FPID Identifies returning visitors so Google Analytics can report on visit patterns over time. — *_FPLC Helps Google Analytics keep a consistent visitor identifier when you move between this site's subdomains or linked domains. — *_FPAU Records which audience segments Google Analytics has assigned to you, used for reporting on visitor groups. — Hotjar Hotjar _hjSessionUser_* Stores a random ID that lets Hotjar recognise you when you return to the site. 365 days _hjSession_* Links the pages you view during one visit to the same Hotjar session. 30 minutes Marketing & Social Media These cookies and similar technologies help advertising and social media partners personalise your experience, show you relevant ads, measure campaign results, and enable sharing features. Google Google _gcl_au Used by Google AdSense for experimenting with advertisement efficiency across websites using their services. 3 months NID This cookies is used to collect website statistics and track conversion rates and Google ad personalisation 1 year Google Analytics FPAU Assigns a specific ID to the visitor. This allows the website to determine the number of specific user-visits for analysis and statistics. Session DoubleClick/Google Marketing IDE This cookie is used for targeting, analyzing and optimisation of ad campaigns in DoubleClick/Google Marketing Suite 2 years Google Ads _gcl_ls This item is used by Google Ads to store advertising click identifiers for conversion measurement. When visitors do not accept tracking cookies, Google can send a cookieless ping via Consent Mode v2 with anonymized data to measure conversions and advertising performance. Data may be stored temporarily or persistently, depending on the implementation. — LinkedIn LinkedIn lidc Used by the social networking service, LinkedIn, for tracking the use of embedded services. 1 day bcookie Used by LinkedIn to track the use of embedded services. 1 year Facebook Facebook _fbp Used by Facebook to deliver a series of advertisement products such as real time bidding from third party advertisers 4 months eur.nl Website *__fbp Stores a Meta (Facebook) browser identifier so visits and conversions can be attributed back to Meta advertising. — *__gcl_au Stores the identifier of the advert you clicked, so a later purchase or sign-up can be credited to the right campaign. — Meta Meta Pixel lastExternalReferrer Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — lastExternalReferrerTime Detects how the user reached the website by registering their last URL-address — Consent dialog opened"
